      "title": "One or more Associate Professors in accounting",
      "description": "One or more Associate Professors in accounting - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy One or more Associate Professors in accounting Apply Vacant position One or more Associate Professors in accounting Aalborg Deadline : 20.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1151 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 20.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1151 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position One or more Associate Professors in accounting Aalborg Deadline : 20.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1151 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 20.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1151 Employment type: Full Time Apply Join an expanding research environment at Aalborg University Business School at the Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, where curiosity, collaboration, and strong academic ambitions shape our work. We are seeking one or more dedicated scholars to help advance accounting research within the Accounting Research Group at Aalborg University Business School. The position is a permanent full time position starting on February 1 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Your work tasks The successful candidate is expected to be committed to research, teaching and supervision, including teaching within AAU's Problem-Based Learning (PBL) approach to contribute to the continued development of accounting education and innovative teaching practices at AAUBS. As an associate professor in accounting, you will conduct independent research and aim for publication in leading international journals. You will be involved in developing and delivering teaching at both bachelor and master levels, and on HD and MBA programs, including a broad array of topics within accounting. The position includes supervision of project groups and individual students, participation in research collaborations within the group, and active engagement in the academic community at the business school. You will be expected to supervise PhD students. You will further contribute to the development of new research ideas and apply for external funding. You will be expected to be present at the business school at least three days again and preferably more to help create a stimulating environment for students and researchers. Your competencies We are looking for one or more colleagues with a strong interest in research and a clear ambition to contribute to international academic debates through rigorous work. We value candidates who are curious, reflective, and open to collaboration, and who enjoy contributing to a collegial research environment. We welcome a broad range of theoretical perspectives and methodological approaches. Experience with teaching at university level is expected. We appreciate a constructive and engaged approach to teaching, supervision, and interaction with students, and we are looking for someone who is motivated to contribute positively to both the research and teaching communities at the business school. Ability to teach in Danish is an advantage. Qualification requirements Appointment as an associate professor requires research and teaching qualifications at the level that can be achieved through the satisfactory completion of a period of employment as an assistant professor but may also be obtained in other ways. It is a precondition that applicants have documented research at an international standard. In addition, applicants are assumed to have received supervision and pedagogical skills development and to have obtained a positive written assessment of their teaching qualifications. Who we are The Accounting research group is based at Aalborg University Business School and has a strong interest in how firms do accounting, and accounting broadly speaking. The group works with contemporary topics in leadership and a broad array of topics within managerial/financial accounting. We value a collegial atmosphere where collaboration, openness, and academic curiosity shape our daily work. Teaching is closely linked to our research activities and to Aalborg University’s long-standing tradition of Problem-Based Learning, which encourages student engagement through project work and real-world analytical challenges. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of ten publications. You must submit a co-author statement, see template for co-author statement Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities . If this is not enclosed, the applicant must enclose the reasons for this Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. The successful applicant is expected, with support from the university, to acquire Danish language skills over time and to be able to contribute to teaching in Danish within 2–5 years of employment, including grading and supervising students, at a level corresponding to the teaching undertaken. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Interviews will be held in November 2026 where the invited candidates will have the opportunity to present their thoughts about and plans for teaching, supervision, research and attraction of external funding. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “ Associate professor . There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Professor, Gunnar Rimmel: +4599409957, gunnarr@business.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1151 Deadline 20.10.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/974224": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in Bioinformatics and Inflammatory Bowel Disease",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Fellow in Bioinformatics and Inflammatory Bowel Disease - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Post-doctoral Fellow in Bioinformatics and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Apply Vacant position Post-doctoral Fellow in Bioinformatics and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Copenhagen Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1158 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1158 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Post-doctoral Fellow in Bioinformatics and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Copenhagen Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1158 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1158 Employment type: Full Time Apply The National Center of Excellence for Molecular Prediction of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (PREDICT), based at Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg University (AAU) in Copenhagen, is looking to recruit a talented researcher for a 3-year, full-time (37 hours per week) postdoc in bioinformatics and IBD from 1 March 2027 or soon thereafter. Your work tasks We are looking to recruit an excellent postdoctoral fellow in bioinformatics with the ambition and skillset to develop their own research projects addressing key research questions within the field of IBD. The research projects can be based on new innovative ways to utilize the many data sources already available in PREDICT, including registry data, genomics, microbiomics, metabolomics and epigenetics.  The postdoc fellow will join a multidisciplinary research environment and work with clinicians and biostatisticians as well as experts in the molecular specialties and is expected to have or obtain expertise in IBD, statistical analysis of several omics data as well as registry data, and contribute with this expertise in collaborations with other disciplines within the center. The postdoctoral fellow will assume primary responsibility for new research projects - from study planning to conducting the study, writing scientific articles, obtaining funding and presenting research at national and international meetings, and training students - while carrying out the transition to becoming an independent researcher. The postdoctoral fellow will refer to Center Director, Professor Tine Jess, and will work closely with the Center's interdisciplinary group of scientists to conduct cutting-edge international research. The workplace will be Aalborg University Copenhagen (Copenhagen South Harbour), where the main facilities of the National Center of Excellence are located. Your competencies We are looking for a candidate with a background in bioinformatics or similar, combined with excellent skills in advanced data analysis, a great insight into molecular medicine, and a special interest in IBD. The ideal candidate has: A PhD in bioinformatics within the field of IBD Has demonstrated expertise in working with registry data as well as genomic, microbiomics and other omics data High-quality publications Experience with project management Excellent writing and communication skills in English Excellent skills in initiating projects and working independently An international network within the field Excellent collaborative skills Who we are PREDICT is at the forefront of international research to unravel the cause and prognosis of inflammatory bowel diseases (IBD), which are chronic and disabling conditions affecting millions of people worldwide. The Center is composed of clinicians, epidemiologists, laboratory, and data scientists working with collaborators nationally and internationally to push the boundaries of precision medicine research and create real-world impact in IBD. We have state-of-the-art facilities within the center and this means through PREDICT you will be part of a well-funded research environment equipped with the latest technologies, unique data, and a world leading network of collaborators. Read more about PREDICT here . About the Department of Clinical Medicine The Department of Clinical Medicine provides research-based teaching across all disciplines of the medical degree programme and conducts research within the clinical specialties. Read more about the Department of Clinical Medicine here Read more about the Department of Clinical Medicine here . We offer We offer an exciting postdoc position in a dynamic, informal, high-performing environment with dedicated, friendly colleagues. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Tine Jess: +4599407804, jess@dcm.aau.dk Gry Juul Poulsen: gryjp@dcm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1158 Deadline 21.10.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/974360": {
      "title": "3-Year Teaching Associate Professorship in Accounting",
      "description": "3-Year Teaching Associate Professorship in Accounting - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy 3-Year Teaching Associate Professorship in Accounting Apply Vacant position 3-Year Teaching Associate Professorship in Accounting Aalborg Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1159 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1159 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position 3-Year Teaching Associate Professorship in Accounting Aalborg Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1159 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 21.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1159 Employment type: Full Time Apply Join an expanding research environment at Aalborg University Business School at the Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, where curiosity, collaboration, and strong academic ambitions shape our work. We are seeking a teaching associate professor to help teach in accounting at Aalborg University Business School. The position is a 3 year full time position starting on February 1 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Your work tasks The job entails teaching and supervision within accounting, particularly valuation and financial analysis. It will be an advantage to be able to teach in Danish. You will be expected to work with the Problem-based learning approach which is the pedagogical approach at Aalborg University Business School. You will be expected to be present at least three days a week at the business school to participate in creating a good learning and research environment for students and researchers. Your competencies We expect you to have a relevant educational background (cand. oecon, cand. merc, or similar) and extensive knowledge of and experience in teaching and supervision at university level. Qualification requirements The qualification requirement for the position is a master’s degree or qualifications of an equivalent level. The applicant's teaching qualifications must also be positively assessed. Who we are The Accounting research group is based at Aalborg University Business School and has a strong interest in how firms do accounting, and accounting broadly speaking. The group works with contemporary topics in leadership and a broad array of topics within managerial/financial accounting. We value a collegial atmosphere where collaboration, openness, and academic curiosity shape our daily work. Teaching is closely linked to our research activities and to Aalborg University’s long-standing tradition of Problem-Based Learning, which encourages student engagement through project work and real-world analytical challenges. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma) Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities. Optional list of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of 5 publications. You must submit a co-author statement, see template for co-author statement. You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Job interviews will be held in the beginning of November 2026. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP ). Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Teaching associate professor”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Lektor, Niels Sandalgaard: +4599408252, nis@business.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1159 Deadline 21.10.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/975532": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Apply Vacant position Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Copenhagen Deadline : 22.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1165 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 22.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1165 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease Copenhagen Deadline : 22.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1165 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 22.10.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1165 Employment type: Full Time Apply The National Center of Excellence for Molecular Prediction of Inflammatory Bowel Disease (PREDICT), based at Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg University (AAU) in Copenhagen, is looking to recruit a talented Associate Professor in Nutrition and Inflammatory Bowel Disease for a full-time (37 hours per week) position from 1 March 2027 to 28 February 2031. Your work tasks The Associate Professor will take primary responsibility for new research projects – from study planning to study conduct, writing of scientific papers, obtaining of funding and presentation of research at national and international meetings, and training of students – while transitioning to become as independent researcher. The successful candidate will also have administrative tasks related to the everyday running of the Center, as part of the team of group leaders referring to the Center Director. The Associate Professor will be referring to the Center Director, working closely with the Center’s interdisciplinary group of scientists to perform forefront, international research. The place of work will be Aalborg University Copenhagen campus (Copenhagen South Harbour), where the core facilities of the National Center for Excellence are located. Your competencies We are looking to recruit an outstanding Associate Professor who is eager to take the lead in the Center’s expertise in nutritional aspect of IBD, including nutritional epidemiology, application of novel molecular approaches within nutritional research, and intervention studies. The Associate professor will perform high impact research on how nutrition influences the development of and disease course in IBD. Examples of study areas include macro and micronutrients, processed foods, food additives and dietary patterns. The Center has access to valuable resources for nutritional epidemiology studies, including biological samples, as well as a high-ranking clinical setting for intervention studies. Who we are PREDICT is at the forefront of international research to unravel the cause and prognosis of inflammatory bowel diseases (IBD), which are chronic and disabling conditions affecting millions of people worldwide. The Center is composed of clinicians, epidemiologists, laboratory, and data scientists working with collaborators nationally and internationally to push the boundaries of precision medicine research and create real-world impact in IBD. We have state-of-the-art facilities within the Center and this means through PREDICT you will be part of a well-funded research environment equipped with the latest technologies, unique data, and a world leading network of collaborators. About the Department of Clinical Medicine The Department of Clinical Medicine provides research-based teaching across all disciplines of the medical degree programme and conducts research within the clinical specialties. Read more about the Department of Clinical Medicine here Read more about the Department of Clinical Medicine here . Qualification requirements Appointment as an associate professor requires research and teaching qualifications at the level that can be achieved through the satisfactory completion of a period of employment as an assistant professor but may also be obtained in other ways. It is a precondition that applicants have documented research at an international standard. In addition, applicants are assumed to have received supervision and pedagogical skills development and to have obtained a positive written assessment of their teaching qualifications. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of ten publications. ***Delete if ENG, TECH, SUND: You must submit a co-author statement, see template for co-author statement Documentation of teaching qualifications. ***Delete the statement that is not relevant, Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, The Faculty of Engineering and Science and The Faculty of Medicine . Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities . If this is not enclosed, the applicant must enclose the reasons for this Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “ Associate professor . There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1165 Deadline 22.10.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
