    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/976015": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, AI, Innovation and Digital Transformation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, AI, Innovation and Digital Transformation - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Assistant Professor, AI, Innovation and Digital Transformation Apply Vacant position Assistant Professor, AI, Innovation and Digital Transformation Aalborg Deadline : 28.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1172 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 28.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1172 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Assistant Professor, AI, Innovation and Digital Transformation Aalborg Deadline : 28.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1172 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 28.10.2026 Department: Aalborg University Business School Ref number: 2026/1172 Employment type: Full Time Apply Do you want to contribute to high-quality research in Generative AI, innovation and the diffusion of digital technologies? Aalborg University Business School is seeking a motivated new colleague for a four-year position as Assistant Professor to join the Innovation, Knowledge and Economic dynamics (IKE) Group. This is a full-time position available from January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Your work tasks We are seeking applicants with a dedicated research agenda on the adoption and diffusion of digital technologies, including AI, and on what they mean for firms, organisations and innovation. Relevant topics include barriers to adoption and implementation, organisational change and the reorganisation of work, capabilities and skills, and public procurement of innovation. As our new colleague, you will join a dynamic research environment and are expected to contribute actively to the continued development of the group's research on technology diffusion and digital transformation. You are also expected to engage actively in joint IKE activities. Your primary research focus will be within innovation and technology dynamics, and we expect you to combine organisational and qualitative insights with computational and data science methods. Within the IKE group, we value a diversity of methodological approaches, spanning from quantitative analysis of register, survey, and patent data to various qualitative methods. If you have an interest in, or experience with, computational social science methods (for example natural language processing, network analysis, or machine learning applied to large text, register and patent data), there is ample opportunity to apply and develop these skills within the group. In addition to research, you will play an important role in our educational programmes. You will deliver teaching at the undergraduate and master’s levels. You will contribute to teaching core disciplines in our bachelor programmes in Economics and Business Administration (HA/EBA) and on the MSc in Economics and Business Administration, in particular the Business Data Science specialisation. Your responsibilities will include lecturing, supervising student projects, and engaging in Problem Based Learning (PBL), which is central to Aalborg University’s pedagogical model. While the position focuses on research and teaching, you will also to a lesser extent undertake coordination and administrative tasks related to your educational obligations.  You will be expected to be present at the business school at least three days a week. Your Competencies We are looking for a colleague with a strong academic foundation and a dedicated research agenda within  generative AI, innovation, technology diffusion and digital transformation. You must have a relevant PhD and competences within Data Science and computational methods. We are particularly interested in candidates who can combine qualitative and organisational research with computational analysis of large-scale data, rather than working exclusively within one of the two traditions. We value candidates who can bridge theoretical concepts with practical application, and it will be an advantage to have a proven track record or a strong inclination towards supervising student projects and designing engaging coursework. For the research aspect, we are looking for candidates motivated to produce internationally recognised work. When you apply for the position as Assistant Professor, we expect you to show high potential and a keen interest in pursuing publications in top-tier journals. On a personal level, we are seeking a team player who will engage actively in joint activities within the IKE Group. You should thrive in a collaborative environment that involves working on externally funded research projects. Regarding language skills, the main working language at Aalborg University Business School is English. Danish language skills are not required at the time of employment. Please note that non-Danish speaking employees will undergo a course in basic Danish language qualifications within the first two years of employment. Qualification requirements Appointment as assistant professor requires academic qualifications at PhD level. The research potential of each applicant will be emphasized in the overall assessment. For the current position, the PhD degree or equivalent documented research training must be within research fields that are relevant to the position and to Aalborg University Business School’s research focus. Who we are You will become part of the Research Group on Innovation, Knowledge, and Economic Dynamics (IKE) at Aalborg University Business School. The IKE Group has a history spanning over 40 years and is internationally recognised for its work on innovation systems, learning economies and industrial dynamics. The group’s research culture emphasizes the interplay between different methodological approaches and fosters a collaborative spirit. We are situated within a Business School that values societal impact and close interaction with the surrounding ecosystem. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. You must submit a co-author statement, see template for co-author statement Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities . Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “ Assistant professor ”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Associate Professor, Roman Jurowetzki: +4599402738, roman@business.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1172 Deadline 28.10.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/954417": {
      "title": "Full professor in Computer Science",
      "description": "Full professor in Computer Science - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Full professor in Computer Science Apply Vacant position Full professor in Computer Science Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/934 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/934 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Full professor in Computer Science Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/934 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/934 Employment type: Full Time Apply Full professor in Computer Science The Department of Computer Science at the Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Aalborg University, is looking to appoint a Full Professor starting April 1, 2027 or soon thereafter. We now welcome strong applicants in all areas of computer science for a new position in Aalborg or Copenhagen. The final application deadline is November 1, 2026. The Department of Computer Science has the following research groups: Automated System Verification and Validation Data Engineering, Science, and Systems Distributed Sustainable Software and Systems Formal Methods for Security and Privacy Foundations for Interacting and Computing Systems Human Augmentation and Collaboration Natural Language Processing Probabilistic and Symbolic AI Physical and Embodied Interaction Quantum Systems Analysis and Synthesis Systems Design & Development Practices Web Science and Engineering Your work tasks We are seeking visionary and internationally recognised scholars who can provide strong academic leadership and drive research excellence within the department. The successful candidate will play a key role in shaping the future direction of research and education, strengthening international collaborations, attracting external funding, and contributing to the continued development of a vibrant and inclusive academic environment. For further information, please contact Head of Department Peter Axel Nielsen at institutleder@cs.aau.dk Your qualifications We are looking for applicants that are able to document a high degree of original academic production at an international level in computer science including supervision of PhD students. Competences and experience from teaching at different levels includes tests/exams, course/study programme management as well as contributions to the development of teaching activities and teaching material. You are a clear communicator and has documented skills as group leader. As a person, you have good interpersonal skills, are inclusive and team-oriented and able to contribute to a good work environment. Emphasis is placed on the extent, to which you have developed the academic discipline from a research and teaching perspective. Emphasis may moreover be placed on the your ability to carry out and develop research-based activities in relation to the university’s external cooperation. The assessment will further be based on these academic criteria. Who we are The Department of Computer Science at Aalborg University is highly regarded in Denmark among researchers, students, and external partners due to its leading research, education, and collaboration activities. The department currently employs more than 165 academic staff and approximately 20 administrative staff and has around 1,100 students. Our research is internationally and nationally recognised as being of the highest standard, prioritising quality over quantity. We balance applications and theory, as well as societal and scientific impact, applying research to solve real-world problems. In addition, we conduct fundamental research with the potential long-term impact. As part of this, we are acknowledged and respected for close collaboration with industry and for applying research to create impact and value for society. Our education is based on problem-based learning and is recognised for producing highly skilled graduates with excellent employability. We apply several pedagogical approaches, including working in multinational teams, integrating research into the curriculum, and using technology in teaching. This creates a unique learning environment that supports student success, fosters an inspiring workplace, and promotes a healthy work-life balance. You can read more on www.cs.aau.dk , and you can read more about the TECH faculty here . Denmark builds on a welfare system, and while taxes are high, there are plenty of welfare services including free education and healthcare including pay during paternity/maternity leave and during sickness. Find more information at the International Staff Unit – they also offer a spouse/partner programme. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of ten publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design . If this is not enclosed, the applicant must enclose the reasons for this. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References (key individuals we can contact for a reference) You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities (the Appointment Order) and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities (in Danish) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities (in Danish). Salary and terms of employment are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) (only in Danish) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities (only in Danish). There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Institutleder: Peter Axel Nielsen: institutleder@cs.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/934 Deadline 01.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/967442": {
      "title": "Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section",
      "description": "Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section Apply Vacant position Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section Copenhagen Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1089 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1089 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section Copenhagen Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1089 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1089 Employment type: Full Time Apply Assistant professor or Assistant professor Tenure Track, Department of Computer Science, Copenhagen Section Department of Computer Science, Aalborg University is hiring Assistant professors or Assistant professors Tenure Track starting February 1, 2027 . The Assistant professor position is a 3-year fixed term full-time position, and the tenure track position, is a structured career pathway with clearly defined criteria for progression to a permanent position upon successful evaluation. One position will be affiliated with the research group Probabilistic and Symbolic AI in the Copenhagen section. One position will be affiliated with the research group Data Engineering, Science, and Systems in the Copenhagen section. About the CPH Section The CPH Section is organised around the Software education programme at AAU’s Copenhagen campus and spans a broad range of computer science research. The two positions in this call will strengthen the section’s profiles in Probabilistic and Symbolic AI (PSAI), covering probabilistic, symbolic and neuro-symbolic approaches to AI, and Data Engineering, Science, and Systems (DESS), focusing on methods and systems for managing and analysing complex data. The section also hosts research in areas including natural language processing and trustworthy AI, human-centred computing, software engineering, and distributed and interactive systems. This breadth supports collaboration across research groups and between foundational, methodological and application-oriented research. The CPH Section is a growing and international academic environment with an informal and collegial working culture. We aim to combine high scientific ambition with openness, mutual respect and a sustainable working life. Staff have substantial academic freedom and responsibility and are encouraged to collaborate across research groups and career stages, contribute to shared research and teaching activities, and develop an independent academic profile. As a member of the section, you will be part of both a close local community in Copenhagen and broader departmental research groups and network. Qualification requirements Appointment as assistant professor requires academic qualifications at PhD level. The research potential of each applicant will be emphasized in the overall assessment. Your work tasks We offer an attractive career opportunity for promising and talented researchers from around the world. The position is a career development position with the possibility of transitioning to a tenured associate professorship. We will work together with you to develop your research talent through supervision, professional networks and pedagogical upgrading. As tenure track assistant professor your primary tasks will be research and research-based teaching. You will teach and supervise students at bachelor’s and master’s level, and you will contribute to the development of the department through research of international quality. In your daily work, you will work closely with both Danish and international colleagues. Your main tasks will consist of: Independent research of the highest international quality including publication. Teaching, guidance and examination of bachelor’s and master’s degree students, as well as possible supervision of PhD students. Some degree of contribution towards attracting external research funding. The opportunity to collaborate with relevant national and international research environments. You will report to the Head of Department Peter Axel Nielsen. Your competencies We are looking for applicants with independent research-related qualifications at a high international level and a PhD degree in computer science or a related field, and you show potential to become one of the best in the academic field of the position. You are a clear communicator with potential of becoming a skilled group leader, and you can, under guidance, organize and conduct supervision and teaching at bachelor’s and master’s degree level. Completed pedagogical courses in supervision or similar will be a plus, as will experience with external research collaborations. We also draw attention to a stay or employment at one or more internationally recognised research institutions. As a person, you have good interpersonal skills, are inclusive and team-oriented and able to contribute to a good work environment. We expect you to be able to write and speak English at the academic level. Tenure track positions are usually aimed at candidates who have not previously held an assistant professor position. In order to be assessed qualified for a tenure track assistant professor position, you must meet these academic criteria . Department of Computer Science Department of Computer Science at Aalborg University is highly regarded among researchers, students, and external partners because of our leading research, education, and collaboration. The department currently has more than 165 scientific staff, 20 administrative staff, and 1100 students. Our research is recognized internationally and nationally to be at the highest level of excellence according to community standards, prioritizing quality over quantity. We balance applications and theory, and societal and scientific impact, applying research to solve real-world problems, while also conducing foundational research with potential long-term impact. As part of this, we are acknowledged and respected for close collaboration with industry and for applying research to create impact and value for society. Our educations are problem-based and recognized for producing highly skilled graduates with very high employability, who are experienced with project work on solving real-world problems in diverse teams and able to think critically about the technologies they develop. You can read more on www.cs.aau.dk , and you can read more about the TECH faculty here . Denmark builds on a welfare system, and while taxes are high, there are plenty of welfare services including free education and healthcare including pay during paternity/maternity leave and during sickness. Find more information at the International Staff Unit – they also offer a spouse/partner programme. Assessment in connection with transfer to associate professorship The assessment in connection with transition to tenure as an associate professor normally takes place in the final six months of the tenure track assistant professors’ employment. However, the employee may request that an assessment take place at an earlier time in the first four years. If this assessment finds that the employee is not academically qualified, they may request another assessment within the final six months of their period of employment. A maximum of two assessments may take place. In order to be qualified for an associate professor position, you must meet these academic criteria . Appointed candidates will have to make a tenure track career plan with the head of department/immediate superior to align expectations and indicate the objectives for the tenure track’s development process. This career plan must be satisfactory followed and accomplished for the tenure track assistant professor to be assessed qualified. Additionally, the assessment, on transition to the associate professorship, will as a minimum, emphasize the following qualifications in relation to the scientific subject area of the tenure track assistant professorship: Research qualifications equivalent to the level that can be achieved on the basis of satisfactorily completed employment as tenure track assistant professor. Documented scientific production at international level. Assessment will be based on up to ten selected publications selected by the employee. Documentation of pedagogical supervision and upgrading of qualifications, including a positive written assessment of teaching qualifications. The assessment will also be based on the employee's teaching portfolio. The level of contribution to an active academic environment as well as the ability to collaborate and build relationships. The level of experience with grant proposals and experience of communicating research to relevant stakeholders. Appointed candidates will have to make a tenure track career plan with the head of department/immediate superior, to align expectations and indicate the objectives for the tenure track’s development process. This career plan must be satisfactory followed and accomplished in order for the tenure track assistant professor to be assessed qualified. If the tenure track assistant professor fails to request that their qualifications be assessed in the last year of their period of employment or if they are assessed as not academically qualified, the university must immediately initiate dismissal proceedings in accordance with the collective agreement rules. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “ Assistant professor ”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Professor Johannes Bjerva: jbjerva@cs.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1089 Deadline 01.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/977747": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients with Atrial Fibrillation and Comorbidities",
      "description": "Postdoc in Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients  with Atrial Fibrillation and Comorbidities - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc in Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients  with Atrial Fibrillation and Comorbidities Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients  with Atrial Fibrillation and Comorbidities Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Health Science and Technology Ref number: 2026/1192 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Health Science and Technology Ref number: 2026/1192 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc in Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients  with Atrial Fibrillation and Comorbidities Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Health Science and Technology Ref number: 2026/1192 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 01.11.2026 Department: Department of Health Science and Technology Ref number: 2026/1192 Employment type: Full Time Apply At the Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology a postdoc in digital education and empowerment for patients with atrial fibrillation and comorbidities are available for appointment from January 1, 2027, or soon hereafter. The duration of the position is three years. The Department of Health Science and Technology (HST) at Aalborg University is an interdisciplinary research and teaching environment where engineering, medicine and health sciences come together to improve people's lives. As a postdoc at HST, you will be affiliated to the Section of Public Health at the Department of Health Science and Technology and become part of an international research community with access to experienced supervisors, modern research facilities and strong interdisciplinary collaboration. You will work alongside researchers from a wide range of disciplines and engage with hospitals, industry and public-sector partners to address some of society's most important health challenges. The department is home to approximately 180 academic staff members, around 100 PhD fellows and more than 1,700 students. We offer a stimulating research environment that encourages scientific curiosity, collaboration and professional development. At HST, our values – Share. Care. Dare. – shape the way we collaborate, support one another and create knowledge with societal impact. Learn more about the department on our website and in our research portal. Your work tasks The postdoc will be affiliated with the research and innovation project AF-EMPOWER: Digital Education and Empowerment for Patients with Atrial Fibrillation (AF) and Comorbidities. AF is one of the most common cardiovascular diseases, is frequently associated with comorbidities such as hypertension, heart failure, obesity, diabetes, and sleep disorders, and AF prevalence is expected to double over the next two decades. Education is a cornerstone of AF care, supporting patient engagement and self-management, yet many patients still report insufficient understanding of their condition and its management. The psychological impact of AF and its comorbidities is increasingly recognized as an important aspect of care. The aim of the AF-EMPOWER study is to co-design, develop, test and evaluate a tailored digital educational and empowerment application for patients with AF and comorbidities and relatives to assess its feasibility, effectiveness, and cost-effectiveness compared with usual care. The postdoc will coordinate and contribute to the co-design process, prototype and program development, feasibility test and evaluation of the effectiveness of the AF-EMPOWER application. You will be involved in data collection, data analysis, and dissemination of research findings. The project combines perspectives from systemic innovation, psychosocial well-being, digital health literacy and equity, behavioural science and patient empowerment, implementation science and mixed-methods evaluation. The Postdoc will work closely with patients with AF, their relatives, healthcare professionals from the Department of Cardiology and the Department of Citizens’ Health at the Regional Hospital in Viborg and Silkeborg, as well as municipalities, general practitioners (GP), community organizations, and researchers. The position requires the ability to work independently, manage multiple tasks, apply for funding and collaborate confidently and effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Applicants should have: A master’s degree and a Phd in health sciences, physiotherapy, nursing, sociology, psychology, or social sciences An interest in co-design, interdisciplinary collaboration, and digital technologies Well-developed skills in conducting research, analyzing data and disseminating results Collaborative competencies to work in an interdisciplinary context A demonstrated track record of securing research funding Language skills in Danish and English (oral and written) Access to a car Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, outlining your motivation for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations In your cover letter, please explain why you find AF-EMPOWER interesting, how your research background can contribute to the project, and which methodological and research skills you would bring to the project. We look forward to receiving your application. You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. The position is subject to a three-month probationary period applicable to both parties. Aalborg University – Knowledge for the World Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer programmes grounded in real-world challenges and produce world-class research through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private organizations. These collaborations generate insights, new solutions to societal challenges, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, with additional campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Professor, Birthe Dinesen: +4520515944, bid@hst.aau.dk HR-employee, Karina Stendahl Jensen: +4599407573, ksj@hst.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1192 Deadline 01.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
