    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/975979": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Position in AI Assistants for Clinical Decision Support",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Position in AI Assistants for Clinical Decision Support - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoctoral Position in AI Assistants for Clinical Decision Support Apply Vacant position Postdoctoral Position in AI Assistants for Clinical Decision Support Aalborg Deadline : 02.11.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1171 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 02.11.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1171 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoctoral Position in AI Assistants for Clinical Decision Support Aalborg Deadline : 02.11.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1171 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 02.11.2026 Department: Department of Clinical Medicine Ref number: 2026/1171 Employment type: Full Time Apply At the Center for Clinical Data Science (CLINDA), Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg University, we are looking for a full time postdoctoral researcher to join us in developing AI-based systems for clinical decision support in hospitals, starting December 1, 2026, or soon hereafter. The duration of the position is two years, with the possibility of extension. Subject Clinical decision support systems can assist healthcare professionals in diagnosing and monitoring health conditions by integrating information from multiple sources, including clinical notes, laboratory and pathology results, imaging (e.g., X-ray, CT, MRI, and PET), clinical guidelines, and coding resources. Such systems can support clinical decision-making by helping clinicians synthesize heterogeneous clinical information and knowledge. Your work tasks The aim of the position is to explore and develop AI agent technologies that can assist healthcare experts in daily clinical problem solving, especially in deciding on the most appropriate next steps in the diagnostic pathway. A central task will be to develop an interactive framework based on large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) techniques, capable of synthesizing information from the diverse data types, and further help interpret the findings in the context of individual patients’ profile and history. Important research questions include how to design the agent framework; how to represent, retrieve, and utilize information from the different data modalities to ground the system’s reasoning in clinical evidence; how to best incorporate human-in-the-loop (HITL) functionality so users can interact with the agent’s reasoning process; and how to enable forecasting and simulations over multiple time steps. The project will be conducted in close collaboration with clinical partners, providing access to data-rich healthcare environments and established diagnostic workflows. One key partner is the Diagnostic Center (DC) in Farsø, Denmark. This setting offers a unique opportunity to develop and evaluate AI-based clinical decision support systems using real-world patient data from individuals undergoing diagnostic evaluation for serious conditions, including cancer and other complex diseases. The position is based in the Clinical AI Group at the Center for Clinical Data Science (CLINDA) , Aalborg University and Aalborg University hospital. The successful candidate will be working in close collaboration with healthcare domain experts from clinical departments at hospitals in the North Denmark Region, including Farsø DC. Your competencies We are looking for a motivated candidate with the following background, skills, and qualities: •    A PhD in computer science or a related field. •    Proven experience in machine learning, where experience in natural language processing (NLP) is highly desirable. •    Experience or education in health data science or a health-related field is a plus. •    Good Python programming skills to implement and prototype research ideas. •    A solid mathematical foundation to support the design and analysis of algorithms and systems. •    Curiosity, motivation, and the ability to communicate clearly. •    An open and collaborative approach to working with health-domain experts, ensuring that research aligns with real-world needs. •    Fluency in written and spoken English. •    As the project will involve working with journal notes written in Danish, proficiency in Danish or another Scandinavian language is a plus, but not a requirement. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. Who we are The position is anchored at the Center for Clinical Data Science (CLINDA) . CLINDA aims to conduct independent research in the development, application, and implementation of data infrastructures for AI-based decision support tools and is rapidly growing with currently more than 20 people. This center provides an excellent environment to conduct innovative research with fellow PhD students, postdocs and more senior researchers, and also promote social interactions. The Department of Clinical Medicine provides research-based teaching across all disciplines of the medical degree programme and conducts research within the clinical specialties. The department collaborates closely with hospitals in the North Denmark Region and general practice in both teaching and research. Medical students receive instruction at several hospital sites and in general practice throughout the region. The department is affiliated with approximately 40 research units, each representing a specific medical specialty. In addition, the department is also associated with several other research units and centres. The majority of the department’s staff hold concurrent clinical positions alongside their academic appointments. Learn more about the Department of Clinical Medicine here . How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) The PhD thesis (if completed at the time of application) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications if relevant. Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the job posting. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Assistant Professor, Hans Moen: +4797502647, hmoen@dcm.aau.dk Associate Professor, Charles Philippe Edouard Vesteghem: +4599407193, cvesteghem@dcm.aau.dk Professor, Martin Bøgsted: +4599403531, m_boegsted@dcm.aau.dk HR Support: +4599403031, aau-hrsupport@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1171 Deadline 02.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/976163": {
      "title": "Postdoc Positions in Natural Language Processing (CPH)",
      "description": "Postdoc Positions in Natural Language Processing (CPH) - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc Positions in Natural Language Processing (CPH) Apply Vacant position Postdoc Positions in Natural Language Processing (CPH) Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1174 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1174 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc Positions in Natural Language Processing (CPH) Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1174 Employment type: Full Time Apply Copenhagen Deadline : 09.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1174 Employment type: Full Time Apply The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Section for Copenhagen, Natural Language Processing The Department of Computer Science at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design invites applications for two or more postdoc positions in the area of Natural Language Processing (NLP). The positions are open for appointments from January 1, 2027 or soon thereafter. The duration of the positions is one or two years, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and preferences. The positions are at AAU’s Copenhagen campus, located at the waterfront in Sydhavnen. The application deadline is Monday, November 9, 2026. Interviews are tentatively planned for December 10, 2026. The positions are hosted within the Natural Language Processing (NLP) research group https://aaunlp.github.io/ at AAU Copenhagen, and postdocs will work under the academic leadership of Professor Johannes Bjerva https://bjerva.github.io/ . The NLP group is a rapidly expanding research environment with strong activities in multilingual NLP, LLM security, linguistically informed approaches to NLP, factuality in LLMs, and socially sustainable AI. The group is supported by several major national and international research grants – in 2026, we have grown to 20 researchers, including a full professor, four assistant professors, one postdoc, two research assistants, and 12 PhD students. As a postdoc, you will join a highly collaborative, international, and ambitious research community, with access to state-of-the-art computational resources. In your role, you will have the opportunity to develop an independent research profile and compete for individual fellowships and faculty positions. The positions include the opportunity to undertake one or more research stays abroad to facilitate knowledge exchange with top research environments worldwide. The positions are in part funded by a DFF: Sapere Aude project (“Building TRUST in Text: Linguistically Motivated Language Model Detection”) Building TRUST in Text: Linguistically Motivated Language Model Detection - Aalborg University's Research Portal , an NNF: Ascending Data Science Investigator project (“LM2-SEC: Linguistically Motivated Language Model Security”) https://vbn.aau.dk/en/projects/linguistically-motivated-language-model-security/ , and an Erasmus+ project on AI-based Personal Language Learning Assistants in collaboration with VSKDansk https://www.brondby.dk/om-kommunen/nyheder/2025/08/vskdansk-far-eu-stotte-til-udvikling-af-ai-baseret-sprogtutor . Your work tasks As a postdoc, you will conduct research within the area of multilingual NLP. We are seeking postdocs with two distinct profiles within this area: • Postdoc 1: Security, Safety, and Privacy in Natural Language Processing and AI, with a focus on Large Language Models (LLMs), LLM-based systems, and Agentic AI • Postdoc 2: AI-based personal language learning assistants (1 year) and AI security (1 year). Furthermore, there will be the possibility to gain experience as a co-supervisor for PhD students associated with these projects, and to supervise students on BSc. and MSc. levels. The positions are embedded in an active and rapidly growing research environment, including ongoing projects on, e.g., AI security, epistemic diversity, linguistically motivated NLP, and knowledge-graph grounded factuality in LLMs. The postdocs will work both independently and collaboratively within the group and will have opportunities to engage with national and international partners. As a part of the projects funding these positions, we will host internationally recognised researchers at AAU, creating additional opportunities for collaboration and knowledge exchange. Your competencies We are looking for candidates motivated to make fundamental scientific contributions to multilingual NLP and AI security. Candidates should have the ambition of reaching an internationally leading level of research excellence by building their own research profile, while contributing to the research environment. Applicants must have: • A relevant PhD degree (e.g., NLP, AI, ML, Security, Cryptography, or a related field) and a relevant MSc degree (e.g., Computer Science, Software Engineering, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Computational Linguistics, or a related field) • Strong skills in machine learning and deep learning • Extensive experience with modern ML and NLP methods, including experience with experimentation, and with publishing in top-tier venues (e.g. ICML, ICLR, NeurIPS, ACL, EMNLP, TACL) • Excellent communication skills in English Applicants with documented experience in security, privacy, safety, or robustness will be preferred. Qualification requirements Appointment as postdoc requires academic qualifications at PhD level. Who we are According to the most recent US News and World Ranking, Aalborg University ranks 4th in Europe and 27th in the world within Best Universities for Engineering. According to a 2018 MIT report, Aalborg University is considered to have the 4th best engineering program in the world. According to the recent Times Higher Education Impact ranking, Aalborg University ranks 9th in the World for UN SDG Impact. The Department of Computer Science at Aalborg University is highly regarded among researchers, students, and external partners because of our leading research, education, and collaboration. The department currently has more than 170 scientific staff, 20 administrative staff, and 1,100 students. Education and research are built around AAU's problem-based learning model. The Section for Copenhagen at the department is a highly collaborative research environment, currently expanding from around 40 employees to approximately 60 over the next few years. The section includes members from research groups within NLP, AI, ML, Databases, Formal Methods, Human-Centred Computing, and others, and is uniquely characterised by an open, friendly, and supportive atmosphere. Daily life in the section is marked by informal interactions, knowledge sharing, and a strong sense of community. We also host a bi-weekly SemiBar (a combined seminar and Friday bar), where staff are challenged to present their research in a manner that provokes discussion across our diverse scientific backgrounds, along with regular social events, reading groups, cross-group research activities, and a newly established local PhD organisation promoting an active social and scientific life among our most junior researchers. Together, these initiatives create a dynamic and welcoming environment for early-career researchers and senior staff alike. The Natural Language Processing (NLP) group, led by Professor Johannes Bjerva, is a rapidly expanding research environment specialising in multilingual NLP, LLM security, linguistically informed AI, and trustworthy language technologies. The group hosts several major research projects funded by, e.g., the Carlsberg Foundation, Danmarks Frie Forskningsfond (DFF), the Novo Nordisk Foundation, and AAU’s AI:X initiative. The group collaborates broadly across Europe and globally, and offers an inclusive, ambitious, and supportive research culture. How to apply Your application must include the following: Cover letter, stating your motivations for applying and your qualifications in relation to the position – at most one page. - Please indicate your preferred starting date, and your preferred duration of employment (at least 1 year, and at most 2 years). - We ask applicants not to use generative AI or writing assistant tools in the preparation of their cover letter, except for basic grammatical and spelling correction. Curriculum Vitae (CV) - at most two pages A full list of publications. - For three of these publications, include a single brief paragraph detailing your contributions to the work. Diplomas (bachelor, master's, and PhD degree diplomas) Project description – at most two pages. Please describe your research vision for the position in relation to the project topics outlined above. Other relevant document You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. International staff are encouraged, with support from the university, to learn Danish during their employment in order to support their integration into the workplace and Danish society. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Professor Johannes Bjerva: jbjerva@cs.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1174 Deadline 09.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/973200": {
      "title": "Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence - HCC - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence - HCC Apply Vacant position Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence - HCC Aalborg Deadline : 13.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1155 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 13.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1155 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence - HCC Aalborg Deadline : 13.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1155 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 13.11.2026 Department: Department of Computer Science Ref number: 2026/1155 Employment type: Full Time Apply Postdoc position in Human-Centred Artificial Intelligence The Department of Computer Science at Aalborg University invites applications for a postdoc position working with Professor Niels van Berkel. The earliest starting date for this position is 1st of January 2027. The project: Safeguarding Users’ Cognitive Autonomy in Human-AI Interaction Cognitive autonomy, our fundamental ability to think independently, is under threat from growing reliance on artificial intelligence (AI) technology. While designed to assist, AI recommendations may inadvertently impede cognitive reasoning and steer decision-making. This raises novel questions about designing systems that assist users while supporting independent thinking. To safeguard users’ cognitive autonomy, this project aims to identify when users’ cognitive autonomy is at risk and how timely digital interventions can support independent thinking. The position is a two-year role and funded by a DFF research project (‘Safeguarding Users’ Cognitive Autonomy in Human-AI Interaction’). Research objectives This project develops methods to detect changes in users' cognitive load and designs digital interventions that support cognitive autonomy , people's ability to think independently, in human-AI interaction. You will connect the project's technical work with its grounding in cognitive theory. The position suits candidates with a PhD in Human-Computer Interaction or a related field who enjoy making empirical, methodological, and technical contributions. You will have the opportunity to shape the project's direction based on your interests. Scientific dissemination is expected to focus on leading Human-Computer Interaction venues. For further information about the project, see: https://dff.dk/en/our-funded-projects/meet-the-researchers/research-leaders/eksterne-personer-en/research-leaders-2026/niels-van-berkel/. Your competencies You hold, or will soon obtain, a PhD degree in human-computer interaction, computer science, applied artificial intelligence, cognitive psychology, or a related field. You demonstrate strong collaboration skills and the ability to acquire new skills and technologies. Outstanding spoken and written communication skills are essential. Qualifications requirements Appointment as Postdoc presupposes scientific qualifications at PhD–level or similar scientific qualifications. If you have not yet completed or defended your PhD degree you can provide confirmation of upcoming graduation from your supervisor or PhD school. The research potential of each applicant will be emphasized in the overall assessment. Appointment as a Postdoc cannot exceed a period of four years in total at Aalborg University. Who we are You will be part of the Human Augmentation and Collaboration research group ( https://www.cs.aau.dk/research/research-groups/human-augmentation-and-collaboration-hac ), an ambitious and supportive research environment in which we design and evaluate interactive systems that extend human cognitive, affective, and collaborative capabilities in digital environments. We frequently publish in the leading venues in Human-Computer Interaction and are supported through a strong network of collaborators. Interested applicants are encouraged to contact the project’s principal investigator, Prof. Niels van Berkel ( nielsvanberkel@cs.aau.dk ), prior to applying to discuss the scientific aspects of the position. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application letter: a maximum two-page letter stating reasons for applying and qualifications in relation to the position. Project description: a maximum three-page description outlining the applicant’s ideas on research directions within the context of the project, including a discussion of relevant related work. A complete list of publications must be attached with an indication of the works the applicant wishes to be considered. You may attach up to 5 publications. List of reference contact(s). Curriculum Vitae (CV). Diplomas Clearly AI-generated application material, as well as applications which fall outside of the project’s scope, will be dismissed. The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Read more about The Technical Doctoral School of IT and Design. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Postdoc”. There is a mutual probationary period of 3 months for the position. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Niels van Berkel: nielsvanberkel@cs.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1155 Deadline 13.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.aau.dk/scientific-positions/show-vacancy/vacancyId/977614": {
      "title": "TENURE TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL BIOTECHNOLOGY",
      "description": "TENURE TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL BIOTECHNOLOGY - Aalborg University Jump to content Vacant positions at Aalborg University Scientific positions Application requirements Recruitment process Career options PhD positions Application requirements PhD Schools Career options Recruitment process Technical or administrative positions Application requirements Appointment and assessment Career options AAU as a workplace Change language DA Search Vacant positions Scientific positions Show vacancy TENURE TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL BIOTECHNOLOGY Apply Vacant position TENURE TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL BIOTECHNOLOGY Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1189 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1189 Employment type: Full Time Apply Vacant position TENURE TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL BIOTECHNOLOGY Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1189 Employment type: Full Time Apply Aalborg Deadline : 15.11.2026 Department: Department of Chemistry and Bioscience Ref number: 2026/1189 Employment type: Full Time Apply The Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Faculty of Engineering and Science, Aalborg University invites applications for one position as tenure track assistant professor within the fields of environmental biotechnology. The positions are open from 1 February 2027, or soon thereafter. Place of the positions is in Section of Environmental Microbiology with workplace in Aalborg, Denmark. Tenure track assistant professors are appointed for a period of six years with the prospect of performance-based promotion to a tenured position as Associate Professor. Tenure track assistant professors are expected to have international academic standing, demonstrating acclaimed competitive research, and/or have a recognized high potential for future impact. Your work tasks At the department we have a strong focus on biotechnological topics within both research and teaching portfolios and this aligns well the visions and sustainability goals of our Faculty of Engineering and Science ( Engineering areas of sustainability ) and the “Knowledge for the World” strategy of Aalborg University ( AAU's Strategy ). Our mission in this regard is to contribute with solutions that enables a sustainable development by management of microbial communities, aid in climate change mitigation, and solutions that reduces biodiversity loss in agricultural and natural systems. The position will have its main emphasis on research and teaching with the areas of environmental biotechnology, microbial ecology and process engineering. The activities will mainly be associated to Center for Microbial Communities (link). We are looking for applicants with documented research and teaching experience within the following research area: Microbial community ecology and process engineering in relation to advanced water/wastewater treatment and/or resource recovery. The tenure track assistant professor’s duties will primarily include theoretical and experimental research within the above field, including contributions to collaborative and interdisciplinary work, obligations with regard to publication/scientific communication and research-based teaching including supervision of project work which is an integrated part of the AAU Problem Based Learning (PBL) approach to teach and supervise students. Your Competencies The tenure track assistant professor must have an academic standing showing internationally competitive research, and/or have recognized high potential to make a future impact. Assessment of applicants will primarily consider their level of documented research. The ability to attract external funding will also be part of the evaluation criteria together with outreach qualifications. Teaching qualifications should be documented, and teaching qualifications and teaching experience are taken into account in evaluating the candidates. Hands-on experience with PBL learning is an advantage. Qualification requirements Applicants for a tenure track assistant professorship must have academic qualifications at PhD level. When appointing tenure track assistant professors, Aalborg University also place particular emphasis on: The candidate can demonstrate a high degree of autonomy in their previous education and employment path The candidate shows considerable research potential and a strong scientific profile with the ability to contribute to interdisciplinary research The candidate has demonstrated experience in the supervision or co-supervision of PhD students. The candidate has academic experience from several universities and/or research institutions and preferably international experience The candidate is a skilled communicator with the ability to communicate complex scientific topics effectively to researchers and practitioners The candidate writes and speaks English at the academic level The candidate is expected to meet the criteria for permanent employment as an associate professor at Aalborg University at the end of the tenure track process Who we are At the Department of Chemistry and Bioscience (BIO), our high-level research spans from basic to applied within both natural sciences and engineering. With approx. 150 employees, 75 PhD students, and 775 bachelor and master’s students at our campuses in Aalborg (main campus) and Esbjerg, we are a vital research and educational institution when it comes to creating new basic knowledge as well as contributing to solving the world’s challenges within biology, chemistry, biotechnology, bioengineering, environmental science, and chemical engineering. We continuously improve our department as an attractive place of work and study. We offer flexible hours, social activities throughout the year both at the department level and in each Section. We are inclusive and have respect for individuals, communities, and cultures. Our work culture is founded on openness, curiosity, transparency, and involvement. Come join us! Read more about the department here; Welcome to the Department of Chemistry and Bioscience - en.bio.aau.dk - Aalborg University Assessment in connection with transfer to associate professorship The assessment in connection with transition to tenure as an associate professor normally takes place in the final six months of the tenure track assistant professors’ employment. However, the employee may request that an assessment take place at an earlier time in the first four years. If this assessment finds that the employee is not academically qualified, they may request another assessment within the final six months of their period of employment. A maximum of two assessments may take place. The assessment, on transition to the associate professorship, will as a minimum, emphasize the following qualifications in relation to the scientific subject area of the tenure track assistant professorship: Research qualifications equivalent to the level that can be achieved on the basis of satisfactorily completed employment as tenure track assistant professor. Documented scientific production at international level. Assessment will be based on up to ten selected publications selected by the employee. Documentation of pedagogical supervision and upgrading of qualifications, including a positive written assessment of teaching qualifications. The assessment will also be based on the employee's teaching portfolio. The level of contribution to an active academic environment as well as the ability to collaborate and build relationships. The level of experience with grant proposals and experience of communicating research to relevant stakeholders. If the tenure track assistant professor fails to request that their qualifications be assessed in the last year of their period of employment or if they are assessed as not academically qualified, the university must immediately initiate dismissal proceedings in accordance with the collective agreement rules. How to apply Your application must include the following: Application, stating reasons for applying, qualifications in relation to the position, and intentions and visions for the position Curriculum Vitae (CV) Diplomas (master's degree diploma and PhD diploma) List of publications, with an indication of the attached publications that you wish to be taken into account in the assessment. You may attach a maximum of five publications. Documentation of teaching qualifications. Please see guidelines for teaching portfolio at The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, The Faculty of Engineering and Science and The Faculty of Medicine. If this is not enclosed, the applicant must enclose the reasons for this . Dissemination qualifications, including participation on committees or boards, participation in organisations etc. Additional qualifications in relation to the position References/recommendations You can read more about the requirements for your application here . The application must be submitted via Aalborg University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aalborg University's website. Aalborg University wants to reflect the surrounding society and has diversity as a core value. Therefore, everyone, regardless of personal background and orientation, is encouraged to apply for the position. Aalborg University has a policy of parallel language use. The successful applicant is expected, with support from the university, to acquire Danish language skills over time and to be able to contribute to teaching in Danish within 2–5 years of employment, including grading and supervising students, at a level corresponding to the teaching undertaken. Danish language courses will be offered as part of the employment. Do you have any questions? If you have any questions about the position, you are more than welcome to contact us. You will find contact persons at the bottom of the jobpost. Further information Read more about our recruitment process here The appointment process at Aalborg University involves a shortlisting process. You can read more about the shortlisting and appointment process here . The hiring process at Aalborg University may include a risk assessment as a tool to identify potential risks associated with new hires, ensuring the safety, compliance, and integrity of the workplace. Salary and terms of employment The employment is in accordance with the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Universities and the Ministerial Order on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Universities. Furthermore, your terms of employment and salary are in accordance with the collective agreement between the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations and the state (AC collective agreement) and protocol on certain terms of employment of academic staff at universities. You can find information about the salary and salary structure for the position in the Salary Overview for Recruitment - Scientific positions (VIP) . Please refer to the introductory section of the page and the section entitled “Tenure track assistant professor/Tenure track researcher”. Aalborg University - Knowledge for the world Aalborg University is an international workplace with more than 3,700 employees. We offer real-world-oriented education and create world-class research results through collaboration between researchers, students, and public and private companies. This is how we achieve insights, new solutions to societal problems, and knowledge that changes the world. Our main campus is in Aalborg, but we also have campuses in Esbjerg and Copenhagen. Contacts Per Halkjær Nielsen: +4599408503, phn@bio.aau.dk HR Support: aau-hrsupport@adm.aau.dk Employment type Full time Ref number 2026/1189 Deadline 15.11.2026 Apply Employment and assessment Contact Contact Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 Fredrik Bajers Vej 7K 9220 Aalborg East - Denmark Tel.: (+45) 9940 9940 aau@aau.dk CVR : 29102384 About AAU About AAU About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact About AAU Contact For alumni For students For staff For PhDs Press contact Shortcuts Shortcuts EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions EAN numbers University Library (AUB) Vacant positions Service About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme About this website Privacy policy, DPO and cookies Accessibility statement Whistleblowing scheme"
    },
